SRR11074216	PRJNA608811	SRP299728	SAMN14088510	SRX7713654	Homo sapiens	ARID1A_CTRL_atacseq_REP1	ARID1A_CTRL_atacseq_REP1	Illumina HiSeq 4000 sequencing: GSM4308124: ARID1A_CTRL_atacseq_REP1 Homo sapiens ATAC-seq	ATAC-seq	GENOMIC	other	SINGLE	ILLUMINA	Illumina HiSeq 4000	Lysis buffer For ATAC-Seq with hSI organoids, organoids were dissociated into single cells and 50,000 cells were lysed in 50 µl cold Lysis buffer (10 mM Tris-HCl, pH 7.4, 10 mM NaCl, 3 mM MgCl2, 0.1% IGEPAL CA-630). After centrifugation at 500 g for 10 min at 4˚C, cells were resuspended in 1X transposition mix (Illumina 25 µl Tagment DNA Buffer, 2.5 µl Tagment DNA Enzyme, 22.5 µl ddH2O) and incubated for 30 min at 37˚C on a shaker at 300 rpm. Immediately after the transposition reaction, DNA was purified using the QIAgen MinElute PCR Purification Kit according to the manufacturer's instructions. Library was amplified with Nextera Sequencing primers in NEBNext Q5 Hot Start HiFi 2X PCR master mix for 5 cycles. To remove large DNA fragments, the PCR reaction was incubated with 0.55X AMPure XP beads (Beckman Coulter) and the unbound supernatant was subsequently purified with QIAgen MinElute coloumns. Again, DNA was amplified with Nextera Sequencing primers in NEBNext Q5 Hot Start HiFi 2X PCR master mix for 9 cycles. Finally, to remove primers and small DNA fragments, PCR reaction was bead-purified with 1.8X AMPure XP beads.	43387149	3355896303	ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR110/016/SRR11074216/SRR11074216.fastq.gz	05e5c88e4e0e036b200a2a72ea81bbdc	2222751403
