SRR11165173	PRJNA608420	SRP250494	SAMN14170003	SRX7789686	Homo sapiens	GW_TGFB_APC_rep2-batch5	GW_TGFB_APC_rep2-batch5	Illumina HiSeq 2500 sequencing: GSM4333336: GW_TGFB_APC_rep2-batch5 Homo sapiens OTHER	OTHER	GENOMIC	other	PAIRED	ILLUMINA	Illumina HiSeq 2500	Viagen Direct PCR Mix Libraries were prepared by PCR amplification of integrated sgRNAs from gDNA. Barcoded primers were used for high throughput analysis of organoid clones. The Illumina TruSeq Nano DNA library prep was used for subquented blunt-ended ligation of sequencing adaptors.	1410378	423113400	ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR111/073/SRR11165173/SRR11165173_1.fastq.gz;ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR111/073/SRR11165173/SRR11165173_2.fastq.gz	64ecbb2d9671a278ffad83d257dc4e9e;ac58bbc01bc0b13f22fe1ad95ea51df7	46270972;63904503
SRR11165182	PRJNA608810	SRP250847	SAMN14112055	SRX7789695	Homo sapiens	APC_0min_cutnrun	APC_0min_cutnrun	Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM4314590: APC_0min_cutnrun Homo sapiens OTHER	OTHER	GENOMIC	other	PAIRED	ILLUMINA	Illumina NovaSeq 6000	MNAse digest 200.000 single cells were harvested from human small intestinal organoids. After two washes, cells were bound to 10 µl of Concanavalin A-coated beads (Bangs Laboratories, cat. no. BP531), diluted in 1ml of binding buffer and rotated 10 min at RT. Cells were cleared on a magnetic rack and beads were resuspended in 50 µl antibody solution. The antibody anti-SMAD3 (1:50, abcam28379 RRID: AB_2192903) was used, and incubated on a rotator overnight at 4˚C. Beads were cleared on a magnetic rack and washed in digitonin buffer before resuspension in 50 µl of digitonin buffer with 700 ng/µl pA-MNase, in order to bind the fusion protein to the antibody. After 1h rotating at 4˚C, beads were cleared on a magnetic rack and washed twice. To activate MNase activity, beads were resuspended in 150 µl digitonin buffer and chilled down to 0˚C before 3 µl of 100 mM CaCl2 were added for 30 min at 0˚C. Reaction was stopped by adding 150 µl of 2X Stop buffer and tubes were incubated for 10 min at 37˚C to release chromatin. After centrifugation for 5 min at 4˚C at 16 000g, tubes were placed on a magnetic rack in order to remove beads. The supernatant was collected and purified using the NucleoSpin PCR clean up kit. DNA was stored at -20˚C before Illumina library preparation.	27554341	8321410982	ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR111/082/SRR11165182/SRR11165182_1.fastq.gz;ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR111/082/SRR11165182/SRR11165182_2.fastq.gz	3688d454358bea706e3c89be67891014;54e1eb12c846c04a5f276db843136700	1567658753;1798866206
